{% doc %}
  Renders one product card (Figma 1:502): square image, sale or sold out badge,
  title link, price and color swatch indicators.

  Every value (image, price, link, selected swatch) comes from the card
  variant: `variant` when passed (a variant item in a multi-source collection,
  TE-3 AC8), otherwise product.selected_or_first_available_variant. When
  `variant` is passed and the product has more than one variant, the variant
  title is a second line inside the title link.

  No JavaScript: the card is one focusable link (the title). The image link is
  aria-hidden with tabindex -1.

  Swatches are indicators, not controls (TE-3 AC2, foundation §9,
  variant-picker §9): the row is aria-hidden, nothing in it is focusable or
  clickable. Colors are chosen in quick view or on the product page. The title
  link reads the number of colors (", 3 colors"). Only option values with a
  native swatch (value.swatch.color or value.swatch.image) are used: the first
  option with more than 1 value where every value has a swatch; otherwise no
  swatches (VP3). Built from option.values, never product.variants (ADR 0008).
  Up to 4 values: all shown. More than 4: 3 shown and "+N" (VP2, TE-3 AC13);
  when the selected value is past the 3rd, it takes the 3rd place so the card
  variant's swatch is always visible (AC8). The swatch of the card variant has
  data-selected. Sold out values are not struck through (variant-picker §9).

  Badge: one `[data-card-badge]` element is always rendered, `hidden` when
  none. Rule: sold_out when the product or the card variant is unavailable;
  sale when compare_at_price > price, label -N% (rounded) or Sale when N rounds
  to 0. When no `variant` is passed and the card variant is not on sale, the
  badge is still sale with label Sale if product.compare_at_price_max >
  product.price_min (another variant is on sale). Sold out also sets
  data-sold-out on the card root: the image is faded (foundation §9).

  New badge (AC-H14, ES1-T174): product tag `new`, lowercase, exact match. Only
  1 badge shows on the start corner, Sold out > -N% > New: CSS hides New while
  `[data-card-badge]` is visible.

  Rating badge (AC-H13): reviews.rating metafield, .value.rating over
  .value.scale_max, brought to a scale of 5 as in blocks/featured-product. It sits
  on the end corner. Without the metafield there is no badge and no default value.
  Star and visible number are hidden from assistive tech; a translated
  visually hidden sentence is read instead.

  Test hooks: product-card, product-card-image, product-card-title,
  product-card-variant-title, product-card-swatches, product-card-swatch
  (data-selected on the card variant's value), product-card-swatch-more,
  product-card-badge(-sale|-sold-out), product-card-badge-new,
  product-card-rating, product-card-rating-value. data-card-link,
  data-card-image, data-card-price, data-card-badge stay for existing tests
  and assets/product-recommendations.js parity; no script reads them on this
  snippet.

  Storefront event shopify:product:view (ES1-T76, TE-4 AC12): the card sits in
  <s-view-event view-event-trigger="intersect"> with product |
  standard_event_data, so the event fires when the card scrolls into view.
  The element is defined by assets/standard-events.js (BE ES1-T81, layout).
  Context: collection (grids) or recommendation (product recommendations,
  ES1-T65); any other value falls back to collection.

  @param {product} product - The product to render
  @param {variant} [variant] - Variant to show. Default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  @param {string} [sizes] - The image sizes attribute. Default: '(min-width: 80rem) 25vw, (min-width: 48rem) 33vw, 50vw'
  @param {string} [loading] - The image loading attribute. Default: 'lazy'
  @param {string} [heading_level] - Tag for the title: h2 to h6. Default: 'h3'
  @param {string} [card_context] - View event context: 'collection' or 'recommendation'. Default: 'collection'
  @param {boolean} [show_swatches] - false: no swatch indicators, for a card fixed to one variant (blocks/bundle-builder). Default: true
  @param {boolean} [show_variant_title] - false: no variant title line even when `variant` is passed (blocks/bundle-builder, Figma 1:636). Default: true

  @example
  {% render 'product-card', product: product %}
  {% render 'product-card', product: product, card_context: 'recommendation' %}
  {% render 'product-card', product: item.product, variant: item, loading: 'eager' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign card_variant = variant | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  assign image_sizes = sizes | default: '(min-width: 80rem) 25vw, (min-width: 48rem) 33vw, 50vw'
  assign image_loading = loading | default: 'lazy'

  assign heading_tag = 'h3'
  case heading_level
    when 'h2', 'h3', 'h4', 'h5', 'h6'
      assign heading_tag = heading_level
  endcase

  assign view_context = 'collection'
  if card_context == 'recommendation'
    assign view_context = 'recommendation'
  endif

  assign card_image = card_variant.featured_image | default: product.featured_image
  assign card_alt = card_image.alt | default: product.title

  # Variant title line (TE-3 AC8): only for a card fixed to a passed variant
  assign variant_title = blank
  if variant != blank and show_variant_title != false and product.has_only_default_variant == false
    assign variant_title = variant.title
  endif

  # Badge of the card variant
  assign badge = 'none'
  assign badge_label = ''
  if product.available == false or card_variant.available == false
    assign badge = 'sold_out'
    assign badge_label = 'products.card.sold_out' | t
  elsif card_variant.compare_at_price > card_variant.price
    assign badge = 'sale'
    assign sale_percent = card_variant.compare_at_price | minus: card_variant.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: card_variant.compare_at_price | round
    if sale_percent > 0
      assign badge_label = 'products.card.sale_percent' | t: percent: sale_percent
    else
      assign badge_label = 'products.card.sale' | t
    endif
  elsif variant == blank and product.compare_at_price_max > product.price_min
    # No variant passed: another variant is on sale (Shopify Theme Store §7)
    assign badge = 'sale'
    assign badge_label = 'products.card.sale' | t
  endif

  case badge
    when 'sale'
      assign badge_testid = 'product-card-badge-sale'
    when 'sold_out'
      assign badge_testid = 'product-card-badge-sold-out'
    else
      assign badge_testid = 'product-card-badge'
  endcase

  assign is_new = false
  if product.tags contains 'new'
    assign is_new = true
  endif

  assign rating_data = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value
  assign rating_value = rating_data.rating
  if rating_value != blank
    assign rating_scale = rating_data.scale_max | plus: 0
    if rating_scale <= 0
      assign rating_scale = 5
    endif
    assign rating_on_five = rating_value | times: 5.0 | divided_by: rating_scale | round: 1
  endif

  # Swatch indicators only from native option value swatches (value.swatch.color
  # or value.swatch.image). VP3: if any value of the option has no swatch, the
  # option prints no swatch on the card.
  assign swatch_option = nil
  if show_swatches != false
    for option in product.options_with_values
      if option.values.size > 1
        assign option_has_swatches = true
        for option_value in option.values
          if option_value.swatch.color == blank and option_value.swatch.image == blank
            assign option_has_swatches = false
            break
          endif
        endfor
        if option_has_swatches
          assign swatch_option = option
          break
        endif
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  if swatch_option
    assign swatch_count = swatch_option.values.size
    assign option_index = swatch_option.position | minus: 1
    assign selected_value = card_variant.options[option_index]

    # VP2: up to 4 shown; more than 4 → 3 shown + "+N"
    assign swatch_visible = 4
    if swatch_count > 4
      assign swatch_visible = 3
    endif
    assign swatch_more = swatch_count | minus: swatch_visible

    # AC8: the card variant's value stays visible, in the last visible place
    assign selected_index = 0
    for value in swatch_option.values
      if value.name == selected_value
        assign selected_index = forloop.index
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}

<s-view-event
  class="product-card__view"
  view-event-trigger="intersect"
  view-event-payload='{{ product | standard_event_data: "view", context: view_context | escape }}'
  data-testid="product-card-view-event"
>
<div
  class="product-card"
  data-testid="product-card"
  data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  {% if badge == 'sold_out' %}
    data-sold-out
  {% endif %}
>
  <div class="product-card__media">
    <a
      class="product-card__media-link"
      href="{{ card_variant.url | default: product.url }}"
      tabindex="-1"
      aria-hidden="true"
      data-card-link
    >
      {%- if card_image -%}
        {{
          card_image
          | image_url: width: 1080
          | image_tag:
            widths: '360, 720, 1080',
            sizes: image_sizes,
            loading: image_loading,
            alt: card_alt,
            class: 'product-card__image',
            data-card-image: 'card',
            data-testid: 'product-card-image'
        }}
        {%- assign hover_media = product.media | where: 'media_type', 'image' -%}
        {%- if variant == blank and hover_media.size > 1 and swatch_option == nil -%}
          {{
            hover_media[1]
            | image_url: width: 720
            | image_tag:
              widths: '360, 720',
              sizes: image_sizes,
              loading: 'lazy',
              alt: '',
              class: 'product-card__image-hover'
          }}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- else -%}
        <span class="product-card__placeholder" data-testid="product-card-placeholder-image">
          {{- 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'product-card__placeholder-svg' -}}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </a>

    <span
      class="product-card__badge"
      data-card-badge
      data-badge="{{ badge }}"
      data-testid="{{ badge_testid }}"
      {% if badge == 'none' %}
        hidden
      {% endif %}
    >
      {{- badge_label -}}
    </span>

    {%- if is_new -%}
      <span class="product-card__badge product-card__badge--new" data-testid="product-card-badge-new">
        {{- 'products.card.new' | t -}}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if rating_value != blank -%}
      <span class="product-card__rating" data-testid="product-card-rating">
        <svg
          class="product-card__rating-star"
          viewBox="0 0 14 13"
          fill="currentColor"
          aria-hidden="true"
          focusable="false"
        >
          <path d="M13.9635 4.91254C13.8718 4.63786 13.6204 4.44277 13.3229 4.41679L9.28214 4.06127L7.68431 0.437487C7.56649 0.171911 7.29817 0 7.00006 0C6.70194 0 6.43362 0.171911 6.31581 0.438108L4.71797 4.06127L0.676558 4.41679C0.379615 4.44339 0.128816 4.63786 0.0366355 4.91254C-0.0555451 5.18723 0.0295857 5.48851 0.254216 5.67843L3.30856 8.27396L2.40791 12.1182C2.342 12.4008 2.45523 12.693 2.69727 12.8626C2.82737 12.9536 2.97958 13 3.13307 13C3.26541 13 3.39669 12.9654 3.5145 12.8971L7.00006 10.8786L10.4843 12.8971C10.7393 13.0457 11.0607 13.0322 11.3022 12.8626C11.5444 12.6925 11.6575 12.4002 11.5916 12.1182L10.6909 8.27396L13.7453 5.67895C13.9699 5.48851 14.0557 5.18775 13.9635 4.91254Z" />
        </svg>
        <span aria-hidden="true" data-testid="product-card-rating-value">{{ rating_on_five }}</span>
        <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.card.rating_label' | t: rating: rating_on_five }}</span>
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <{{ heading_tag }} class="product-card__title">
    <a
      class="product-card__link"
      href="{{ card_variant.url | default: product.url }}"
      data-card-link
      data-testid="product-card-title"
    >
      {{- product.title | escape -}}
      {%- if variant_title != blank -%}
        <span class="visually-hidden">, </span>
        <span class="product-card__variant" data-testid="product-card-variant-title">{{ variant_title | escape }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if swatch_option -%}
        <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.card.color_count' | t: count: swatch_count }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </a>
  </{{ heading_tag }}>

  <div class="product-card__price" data-card-price>
    {%- render 'price', product: product, variant: variant -%}
  </div>

  {%- if swatch_option -%}
    <div class="product-card__swatches" aria-hidden="true" data-testid="product-card-swatches">
      {%- for value in swatch_option.values -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign show_value = false
          if selected_index > swatch_visible
            if forloop.index < swatch_visible or forloop.index == selected_index
              assign show_value = true
            endif
          elsif forloop.index <= swatch_visible
            assign show_value = true
          endif
        -%}
        {%- if show_value -%}
          <span
            class="product-card__swatch"
            data-testid="product-card-swatch"
            {% if forloop.index == selected_index %}
              data-selected
            {% endif %}
            {% if value.swatch.image %}
              style="--swatch-image: url({{ value.swatch.image | image_url: width: 64 }});"
            {% else %}
              style="--swatch-color: {{ value.swatch.color }};"
            {% endif %}
          >
            {%- if forloop.index == selected_index -%}
              <span class="product-card__swatch-tick"></span>
            {%- endif -%}
            <span class="visually-hidden">{{ value.name | escape }}</span>
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}

      {%- if swatch_more > 0 -%}
        <span class="product-card__swatch-more" data-testid="product-card-swatch-more">
          {{- 'products.card.more_swatches' | t: count: swatch_more -}}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
</s-view-event>
